  {"comment":"SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT. A pattern of a pattern of a sheet metal body makes sheets (mitcad#1462): t=1, r=1, K=0.4. A 40 x 20 panel folded 90 degrees at x=30 (800 + pi), patterned along y by 30 (a sheet copy, mitcad#1450); a mirror of that pattern about x=0 copies the body as it was before the pattern at both of its places: F7.b0 at y=0..20 and F7.b1 at y=30..50, each a sheet whose panels keep their identities. A Fold on F7.b1 at x=-10 turns its outer 20 mm: 800 + 2 pi. Then a flat panel patterned along y and the pattern mirrored with Join: the copy at the original's place joins it into one sheet (1600), the other copy is a sheet of its own."},
